# Formatting

After a closing `}` that ends a block, put a blank line before the next statement. Do not put a blank line between `}` and `else` / `catch` / `finally`, or immediately before a parent `}`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
for (const table of tables.values()) {
  destroy(table);
}
tables.clear();

// ✅ GOOD
for (const table of tables.values()) {
  destroy(table);
}

tables.clear();
```
